PE 809: Rational Polynomials / 有理多项式

=== Rational Function Iteration ===
Given rational function R(x) = P(x)/Q(x), iterate:
  x_{n+1} = R(x_n)

=== Example: f(x) = 1 + 1/x ===
x_0 = 1/1 = 1.000000
x_1 = 2/1 = 2.000000
x_2 = 3/2 = 1.500000
x_3 = 5/3 = 1.666667
x_4 = 8/5 = 1.600000
x_5 = 13/8 = 1.625000
x_6 = 21/13 = 1.615385
x_7 = 34/21 = 1.619048
x_8 = 55/34 = 1.617647
x_9 = 89/55 = 1.618182
x_10 = 144/89 = 1.617978

=== Möbius Transformations ===
Any rational function of degree 1 is a Möbius transformation:
  f(x) = (ax + b) / (cx + d)
The iteration of Möbius transformations relates to matrix powers
and can be analyzed via eigenvalue decomposition.

=== Problem Context ===
The problem likely studies rational polynomial sequences
with constraints on when terms become integers, or
counting/summing properties of such sequences.

